node_modules/
dist/
*.vsix
.vscode-test/
.claude/
# docs/ is local-only by default: working notes and design history never land
# in git (plans belong in PR descriptions). Tracked exceptions:
docs/*
# Per-code diagnostic explanations (README + diagnostic codes link to it).
!docs/diagnostics/
# The layout-calibration evidence + GUI editor ledgers (see its README.md).
!docs/gui-designer/
# Per-release notes: release.yml reads docs/release/<version>.md as the
# GitHub Release body and the Discord announcement.
!docs/release/
# The wire contract external clients code against — public, versioned.
!docs/PROTOCOL.md
# The guide for applications embedding the server; public, linked from the
# server README.
!docs/EMBEDDING.md
# What a workspace costs and how to configure a big one; public, linked from
# the extension README and the CHANGELOG.
!docs/PERFORMANCE.md
# Features hidden from users until they are fleshed out; code comments point
# at it, so it travels with the repo.
!docs/deferred-features.md
# The release runbook (AGENTS.md points at it).
!docs/RELEASING.md
# How the per-language file icons are generated and verified.
!docs/file-icons.md
# The webview panel pattern and the checklist for adding one (CONTRIBUTING.md
# points at it).
!docs/webviews.md
# Machine-specific paths for scripts/tests (copy dev-paths.example.json).
dev-paths.json
# Build-time copy of the server bundle data (scripts/copy-server.mjs).
packages/vscode/data/
packages/vscode/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md
*.tar.gz
px-lsp-win-x64-*.zip
# Checksum-verified nodejs.org download cached by scripts/build-server-zip.mjs.
.cache/
scripts/nvim-parity/results.json
